are here, so Ainsley, Emma, Pam, and Lisa

00:12:38.949 --> 00:12:45.100
right here in the front row. They're
gonna hang out. No, these

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:49.120
people are amazing! They've taught me if
you think that this event went smoothly

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:54.339
it's because they taught me how to do it.
You know they're amazing and they're

00:12:54.339 --> 00:12:58.690
hanging out for this morning so if
anybody wants wants to talk about how to

00:12:58.690 --> 00:13:01.839
leverage development or how to think
about development in your context

00:13:01.839 --> 00:13:05.620
they're gonna be hanging out ready to
brain dump on you if that is something

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:09.220
that you want to talk about. So I'm gonna
leave it at that. Grant how are we

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:13.089
with time? Great, so if anybody wants to
hand over some questions I'm happy to

00:13:13.089 --> 00:13:16.620
